Windows + exFAT-formatted drives don't support symlinks/reparse points, so
checkpointing crashes trying to create checkpoints/last as a symlink. This
falls back to a real directory copy when symlinking isn't supported. Apply
to src/lerobot/common/train_utils.py, function update_last_checkpoint().
Only needed if your training output directory lives on an exFAT drive
(common for external/portable drives on Windows); NTFS and Linux/macOS
filesystems don't need this.

--- a/src/lerobot/common/train_utils.py
+++ b/src/lerobot/common/train_utils.py
@@ -88,7 +88,12 @@ def update_last_checkpoint(checkpoint_dir: Path) -> Path:
         shutil.rmtree(last_checkpoint_dir)
     relative_target = checkpoint_dir.relative_to(checkpoint_dir.parent)
-    last_checkpoint_dir.symlink_to(relative_target)
+    try:
+        last_checkpoint_dir.symlink_to(relative_target)
+    except OSError:
+        # Some filesystems (e.g. exFAT-formatted drives on Windows) don't support
+        # symlinks/reparse points at all. Fall back to a real copy so
+        # `checkpoints/last/pretrained_model` still resolves for eval/rollout.
+        shutil.copytree(checkpoint_dir, last_checkpoint_dir)
